EVALUATION.md §8.1, §8.3, TYPES.md §12.1 (DECISIONS 226): a check written in a variant body
outside any case runs on every case value, before the case's own checks; a false one is reported
at the instance (the case name of its literal), relates its declaration and carries its name.
-- teamboard/rewards.canon --
package teamboard

variant Reward {
  gold {
    amount: Int

    check capped: amount < 100 else "too much gold"
  }
  nothing

  check spent: self.kind == nothing else "an unspent reward"
}

let rewards: [Reward] = [gold { amount: 500 }, nothing]
-- findings.txt --
error[E5001]  teamboard/rewards.canon:14:26
  rewards[0]: an unspent reward
  expected by teamboard/rewards.canon:11 (check spent)

error[E5001]  teamboard/rewards.canon:14:26
  rewards[0]: too much gold
  expected by teamboard/rewards.canon:7 (check capped)

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
